WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.065
Cross the line and Results opens: where you finished, and what to ride next.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.471
Against bots it reads your place out of ten, in volt on the podium, with your time.

00:00:15.471 --> 00:00:20.919
Below, the final standings: every rider with a time, bots marked, your row current.

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:30.671
Finish sixth and it says how far off: twenty-seven thirty-two, eighteen seconds off

00:00:30.671 --> 00:00:31.615
the podium.

00:00:38.714 --> 00:00:43.425
Against your best it shows the time. A class shows thirty minutes, three hundred

00:00:43.425 --> 00:00:46.964
forty-two kilojoules and eighty-four percent on target.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.675
Done goes home. Race it again opens Race Setup with the same mode and pack; Ride it

00:00:56.675 --> 00:00:58.011
again, the class.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.715
What the tests prove: a real race and class end on Results, every line of the view,

00:01:06.715 --> 00:01:07.993
and the way back.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
